 {"id":"fabro-ee5d","title":"fabro_run_wait until=merged returns blocked immediately; conductor misjudges successful merge pass as \"Merge child failed\"","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T13:53:47.604Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T15:25:10.439Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"fabro_run_wait until=merged returns blocked immediately; conductor misjudges successful merge pass as \"Merge child failed\"\n\nSYMPTOM (conductor run 01M20DMYEK5B3GDQAYFR83DNGN, pass 11:49 2026-09-08):\nmerge child 01M20E43YS004DCEYPJ0GJQH4B succeeded and opened PR #64, but the conductor merge leg labeled \"Merge child failed\" and parked at the kind=\"soft\" exit (failed/soft_stop). The PR merged seconds later (squash commit 9613ec4d8) - the pass was actually successful. Reproduced identically at 14:00 (child 01M20N60ZY6DZDTX60WW0161KP, PR #65, conductor 01M20N33G1T3MHVAJ4T3KJ1NRG).\n\nEVIDENCE (conductor events, run 01M20DMYEK5B3GDQAYFR83DNGN):\n- seq 75/76: fabro_run_wait {run_id: child, timeout_ms: 2400000, until: \"terminal\"} -> reached=terminal, status succeeded. Correct.\n- seq 80/81: fabro_run_wait {run_id: child, timeout_ms: 1200000, until: \"merged\"} -> reached=blocked IMMEDIATELY (child completed 12:07:09, stage concluded ~12:07:3x). PR #64 existed at that point with auto-merge pending. The wait should have polled until the 20-min timeout or the merge, not returned blocked at once.\n- The merge-leg journal: \"returned reached=blocked on the first wait call (~immediate); merge gate stuck - failed required checks or dirty/blocked base. Never re-wait (fabro-bde4).\"\n\nHYPOTHESIS: the until=merged wait path treats a PR whose merge is merely PENDING (checks running / auto-merge enabled but not yet merged) as blocked, instead of waiting. Likely in the wait/merge-detection implementation (server run_wait handler or its GitHub merge check).\n\nACCEPTANCE: until=merged with a 20-min timeout keeps polling while the PR is open, auto-merge-enabled, and not failed; blocked only on a terminal unmergeable state (failed required checks, conflict, closed). Add a regression test with a PR that merges 30s after terminal.\n\nNOTE: secondary effect - Failed{SoftStop} counts as a breaker failure for the schedule breaker (3 consecutive same-signature pauses the trigger). A conductor that soft-parks normally must not get its cron paused; revisit counts_as_breaker_failure if soft parks stay common.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
